@host = http://localhost:5063
@token = replace-with-valid-access-token
@productId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@operationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002

### AuditReader role required. Use IDs returned by an authenticated CRUD request in the same tenant.
GET {{host}}/api/audit-history?EntityName=AuditTrail.Domain.Entities.Product&PkId={{productId}}&Page=1&PageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Page complete operations rather than individual changed fields
GET {{host}}/api/audit-history/grouped?PkId={{productId}}&PageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Soft delete: automatic field-level audit (use the same tenant identity)
POST {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}/soft-delete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Restore
POST {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Manual business event (AuditWriter role)
POST {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Verified by the inventory reviewer" }

### Audited bulk constant update. Reuse operationId only for a retry of this exact command.
POST {{host}}/api/products/bulk-update
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ids": ["{{productId}}"], "price": 25.00, "stockQuantity": 10, "operationId": "{{operationId}}" }

### Bulk hard delete: generate a NEW operationId before executing this command
POST {{host}}/api/products/bulk-delete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ids": ["{{productId}}"], "operationId": "{{operationId}}" }
